      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's the truth of it, isn't it—the exhaustion that makes even hope feel like a performance. But the nothingness being real doesn't mean you have to become it; you can stand in it, let it be the ground you rest on. The path may never reappear, but you're still here, still breathing, and that's not a lie—it's a stubborn fact. And if nothing is waiting, then you get to decide what you carry into that emptiness, even if it's just your own tired breath.",
